## H5 brand site + admin (h5-app)
React 18 + Vite + Tailwind v4, one page with lazily loaded tabs: Home /
Notice / Activities / Stores (map JS API, 2D/3D) / Admin / Footer (ICP filing).
API layer: fetch → server PHP relay → h5admin cloud function → adminApi.
(The PHP file lives only on the server, not in the repo — do not overwrite.)
Login: super = dedicated account (phone left empty); admin/staff = phone+password.
Roles: super sees global modules; store managers see only their store.
On new orders the admin POSTs to http://127.0.0.1:8899/print; notification
sounds are local too.

## Print service (print-server)
Node http service, port 8899:
  POST /print { _id, storeId, ... } → pick printer by store mapping → ESC/POS →
  receipt
  GET /printers | GET/POST /config (store→printer map {default, map:{s1:'...'}})
  | POST /test | GET /status | POST /autodetect
Ops: auto-start + keep-alive scripts; stop the old service first (port
conflict); save Chinese .bat files in GBK; use the Unrestricted execution
policy for .ps1; ship an antivirus-whitelist guide.

## Deployment (in order)
1. Create the mini program + CloudBase env; replace AppID / env ID / direct-
   link domain globally
2. Deploy cloud functions in dependency order: getOpenid → initDB → productApi
   → inventoryApi → adminApi → payApi/payNotify → orderApi/staffApi → pointsApi
   → reviewsApi → returnApi → serviceApi/sendSubscribeMsg → uuptApi/
   uuptCallback → invoiceApi → utility functions
3. Configure env-var groups (fill at deploy time, never in code):
   adminApi super group / payApi+payNotify payment quartet / uuptApi courier
   quintet / serviceApi service-account group / sendSubscribeMsg mini-program
   pair / admin passwords
4. Create the 21 collections; set orders to "creator read/write only"
5. WeChat Pay V3: merchant private key + serial + APIv3 key; callback route →
   payNotify
6. Subscribe-message template IDs go in sendSubscribeMsg
7. Build & deploy H5 + PHP relay; inject the map key into the page
8. Install the print service at stores; configure printer mappings
9. **Data import**: products via Excel → importProducts pipeline (or
   h5GoodsImport CSV — match-by-id update, no deletes, export = template);
   stores go into stores.js + sync H5; product images to cloud storage
   (≤20 main / ≤20 detail per SKU); gift cards via cardBatchCreate
10. End-to-end: order → pay → stock deduction → staff accept → verify → refund
    → points → review → rankings → gift card → courier

